"hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:"
1728,"###
 Al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman al-Muradi narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Wahb informed us, stating: Ibn Abi al-Zinad informed me, from his father, from Musa ibn Abi Uthman, from Abu Hurayrah (RA), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""The master of the days is Friday. On it, Adam was created, on it he was admitted into Paradise, on it he was expelled from it, and the Hour will not be established"
1729,"Narrated to us Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ad-Dawraqi, who narrated to us Muhammad ibn Mus'ab (i.e. al-Qurqusa'i), who narrated to us al-Awza'i, from Abu Ammar, from Abdullah ibn Farrukh, from Abu Hurairah (RA), from the Prophet (ﷺ). The Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""The best day on which the sun has risen is Friday. On it Adam was created, on it he was admitted to Paradise, on it he was expelled from it, and on it the Hour will be established.""

[Commentary from the hadith compiler:] Abu Bakr stated: There is disagreement regarding this phrase, from his (ﷺ) statement: ""On it Adam was created"" up to ""and on it the Hour will be established"" – is this narration from Abu Hurairah (RA) from the Prophet (ﷺ), or from Abu Hurairah (RA) from Ka'b al-Ahbar? I have compiled these reports in my book *al-Kabir*, grouping those who attributed this statement to Abu Hurairah (RA) from the Prophet (ﷺ) and those who attributed it to Ka'b al-Ahbar. My inclination leans towards the narration that attributes this statement to Abu Hurairah (RA) from Ka'b, because Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah (RA): ""The best day on which the sun has risen is Friday. On it Adam was created, on it he was made to dwell in Paradise, on it he was expelled from it, and on it the Hour will be established."" He (the intermediate narrator) said: I asked him (Abu Hurairah): Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)? He replied: Rather, Ka'b narrated it to us. This same narration is also reported by Aban ibn Yazid al-Attar and Shu'ban ibn Abd al-Rahman an-Nahwi, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir.

Abu Bakr added: As for the statement ""The best day on which the sun has risen is Friday"", this is definitively from Abu Hurairah (RA) from the Prophet (ﷺ), with no doubt or uncertainty in it. The additions that come after it: ""On it Adam was created"" up to the end of the statement – this is the point of disagreement among narrators: some say it is from the Prophet (ﷺ), while others say it is from Ka'b al-Ahbar."
